## Compiled, runnable original (for headless simulation / ground-truth checks)

A real installed copy of the original app — not just decompiled source — lives at:

- Root: `D:\Work\TDE\Chargen`
- Compiled app jar: `D:\Work\TDE\Chargen\chargen.jar` (contains the real compiled classes **and** the bundled game-data XML as classpath resources, e.g. `de/bernhardjung/dsaprogramm/daten/rassen/Elfen.ras`)
- Runtime dependency jars: `D:\Work\TDE\Chargen\lib\*.jar` (`nanoxml-2.2.3.jar`, `forms-1.2.0.jar`, `itext-2.0.6.jar`, `jhbasic-2.0.02.jar`, `swing-layout-1.0.2.jar`)
- Launcher: `D:\Work\TDE\Chargen\chargen.exe`

This lets you get **exact ground truth by running the real bytecode** (`javac`/`java -cp chargen.jar;lib\*`) instead of re-deriving GP/AP/SKT formulas by hand from decompiled source — useful whenever a task needs to verify or simulate character creation costs against the original tool. `Erschaffung.debugSchnellerschaffung(rasseId, kulturId, professionId)` is a public headless entry point (no GUI dependency) for scripting a race/culture/profession build directly.

The web Player Character Generator under Tools (`lib/chargen/`, `/tools/player-character-generator`) is the port of this tool. Prefer matching its data IDs, wizard flow, and sheet layout over inventing new ones.
